# Chess Assist — Use Warning and Disclaimer

**Effective date: October 29, 2026**

This document explains risks associated with Chess Assist (the “Software”), including its browser extension, userscripts, bookmarklet, and related source files. It is a warning and disclaimer, not a set of restrictions on how you choose to use the Software. Your use is your choice and responsibility.

## Platform rules and account risk

Chess Assist can use Stockfish to analyze positions, suggest moves, display analysis, and make moves automatically. Chess.com’s [Fair Play rules](https://support.chess.com/en/articles/8568369-what-do-i-need-to-know-about-fair-play-on-chess-com) prohibit outside assistance, including chess engines, software, bots, plugins, browser extensions, and tools that analyze positions during Live Chess. Using Chess Assist in an ongoing game against another person may violate those rules and can result in a ban, account closure, rating or result changes, or other action from Chess.com.

You decide whether to use the Software and accept the risks of that choice. This document does not grant permission from Chess.com or change its rules. Other websites, tournaments, and organizers may have their own rules and may take their own action.

